    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol4_photocopier_drone.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "interlude",
      "text": "generation loss",
      "sub": "copy shop · issue six · the ruined future · 1945",
      "duration": 2000
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "[shot:insert page]Four in the morning at the copy shop. The first page of a pulp story goes under the lid and comes out warm."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "The sky was falling and it came down in pieces."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Copy the copy."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "The sky was falling and it came down in pieces. Grainier now."
    },
    {
      "t": "cg",
      "src": "assets/cg/vol4_meld_facet_xerox_pulp.jpg",
      "caption": "halftone, second generation"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Jack Perkins crouched under a fallen street sign, thick cables held at odd angles. In the copy the cables look like the rules on a zine page, and the street sign could be a masthead."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Copy the copy."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "He stuck out like a shiny quarter in a penny jar."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "The machines drifted above covered in tiny lights like little eyes. On the copy they're just more dots."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol3_ruined_city_night.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol4_radio_static.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "interlude",
      "text": "transmission",
      "sub": "the ruined future · copy shop · ——",
      "duration": 1800
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "A voice came booming from a machine among machines."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Crackle like static electric, welcome to this world of mine."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol4_bus_station_day.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol4_city_pulse.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "show",
      "char": "charlie",
      "expr": "neutral",
      "pos": "center"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "At a bus station a man stands reading his newspaper, his name printed on the newspaper itself."
    },
    {
      "t": "say",
      "char": "Charlie",
      "expr": "tired",
      "text": "We all just want her out of our heads."
    },
    {
      "t": "hide",
      "pos": "center"
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol4_office_copier.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol4_photocopier_drone.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Copy the copy."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Mistakes are like children, hard to take back."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "[shot:insert glass]Last pass comes out nearly black, the whole ruined city one field of toner, and a white line down the middle where the glass is scratched."
    },
    {
      "t": "flag",
      "key": "meld_facet_xerox",
      "val": true
    },
    {
